+# Production roles and override workflow (recommended)
+
+Roles
+- Platform Owner: authority to sign override artifacts (COSIGN KMS principal). Approves emergency promotions and signs override artifact.
+- Safety Officer: approves and reviews HIL/failure triage & formal mitigations.
+- Controls Lead: responsible for RT/HIL remediation and controller fixes.
+- Perception Lead: responsible for OOD triage and retrain/hardening.
+- Infra Operator: provisions and hardens runners/builders, installs vendor SDKs and maintains CI secrets.
+
+Override workflow (carbon / emergency promotions)
+1. Platform Owner composes override using ops/carbon/override_signer.py and COSIGN_KMS_URI.
+2. Platform Owner stores the signed override artifact in a known S3 location or provides to CI run input.
+3. CI promotion gate verifies override via cosign verify and records override artifact via evidence_sdk.
+4. Each override is logged and retained per evidence retention policy for audit review.
+
+Auditing
+- All overrides must include reason, expiry, and approver in the approval artifact and be retained 365 days.
+- Monthly review by Platform Owner and Safety Officer.
+
